\subsection{Method \code{compute_dynamic_sn_ratio()}}{
Compute the dynamic Signal-to-Noise ratio for a Taguchi
experiment with a signal (input) factor. The dynamic SN ratio
evaluates the input-output (linear) relationship between the signal
factor \code{M} and the response \code{y}. Two reference models are
supported: \code{"zero_point"} (zero-point proportional,
y = beta * M, the most common dynamic Taguchi model) and
\code{"linear"} (reference-point proportional, y = beta0 + beta1 * M).
\subsection{Usage}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}\preformatted{TaguchiAnalyzer$compute_dynamic_sn_ratio(y, M, type = "zero_point")}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}

\subsection{Arguments}{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
\describe{
\item{\code{y}}{Numeric vector of response values.}

\item{\code{M}}{Numeric vector of signal-factor values (same length as y).}

\item{\code{type}}{Character scalar giving the dynamic model:
\code{"zero_point"} or \code{"linear"}.}
}
\if{html}{\out{</div>}}
}
\subsection{Returns}{
Numeric scalar giving the dynamic S/N ratio (dB).
}
}
